# ON_BLOCK — he raises it and BLOCKS a hit, and the wish rides the block. A real shield, built
# with base_item: vanilla raises it and blocks exactly as it always does, and WishShapeEvents runs
# act() as him each time it actually stops a hit. A wish about him happens on him; one about
# something else happens a few steps along his line of sight, as for a right-click (the AIM line).
import common

function give()
${GIVES}
    /tellraw @s {"text":"${GIVE_MESSAGE}","color":"${HEX}"}
end

function act()
    ${AIM}
end

${EFFECT_BLOCK}
